course: dictionary
lesson: 5293
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. «The garage was full of junk: old bikes, broken chairs and boxes nobody wanted.» Here junk means old things that are not wanted or have no use. The clues are old, broken and nobody wanted.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «One treat meal is fine, but a huge pile of junk food is not good for you.» Here junk food means food with lots of sugar, salt or fat and little goodness. The words food and not good for you are the clues.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Old things nobody wants" does not fit well into "a huge pile of junk food", so that is not the right meaning here. Try another meaning and see if the sentence now makes sense.
fact: Junk, as a noun, means old things that are not wanted, are broken, or have no use.
fact: Junk food is food with lots of sugar, salt or fat and little goodness.
fact: Junk mail is advertising you did not ask for, on paper or by email.
fact: «Space junk» means broken satellites and pieces orbiting Earth very fast, and even a fleck of paint can damage a spacecraft.
fact: Informally, to junk means to throw away, and a junk is also a kind of wooden sailing boat from China.
exercise: «The garage was full of junk.» What does junk mean here? | A wooden sailing boat from China | * Old things that are not wanted | Food with lots of sugar | Brand new tools for the car
exercise: «Too much junk food is bad for your health.» What does junk food mean? | * Food with lots of sugar, salt or fat and little goodness | Food made from fresh fruit and vegetables | Food for a picnic | Food that is cooked in a box
exercise: «Junk mail arrived again today, and nobody asked for it.» Which is junk mail? | A letter from your best friend | A parcel you ordered online | * Advertising you did not ask for
test: «Space junk is broken satellites orbiting Earth very fast.» What is space junk? | * Broken satellites and pieces orbiting Earth | Brand new spaceships on the launch pad | A moon of Mars | A kind of sweet from the shop
test: Dad says, «I'll junk these old shoes.» What does junk mean here? | Polish them until they shine | Keep them for a special day | * Throw them away | Wear them to the park
exam: «Junk email can be a scam, so do not click its links.» What should you do with a junk email that has links? | Reply and ask for more | Click every link to check it | * Do not click the links | Forward it to all your friends
